# Keep the Docker build context small. deploy/Dockerfile.server uses `COPY . .`, so without this the
# host's multi-GB Rust build artifacts (target/) get dragged into the context on EVERY build — which
# fills the Docker disk and corrupts the image store. Exclude build artifacts + VCS history; the
# Dockerfile rebuilds everything it needs inside the image from the source it explicitly copies.
target/
**/target/
.git/
